WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.900
A pill taken for acne can change how a baby's face forms.

2
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.440
How can a drug for the skin reach the face?

3
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.960
Look at the hindbrain of an early embryo.

4
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.500
It shows a row of small bulges, called rhombomeres.

5
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.460
Early on, their cells look much alike.

6
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:29.160
Yet r2 will make the motor neurons that work the jaw, and r4 those that move the

7
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.960
face. Each bulge needs an address.

8
00:00:32.883 --> 00:00:37.463
The address starts with a vitamin A product, retinoic acid.

9
00:00:38.283 --> 00:00:44.543
An enzyme called Raldh2 makes it in tissue beside the hindbrain and spinal cord.

10
00:00:45.643 --> 00:00:49.323
Enzymes called Cyp26 destroy it toward the front.

11
00:00:50.443 --> 00:00:54.323
Think of a bath with the tap at one end and the drain at the other.

12
00:00:55.283 --> 00:01:01.043
Retinoic acid ends up high toward the back of the hindbrain and low toward the front.

13
00:01:01.083 --> 00:01:05.783
Retinoic acid is small and oily, so it reaches the nucleus.

14
00:01:06.643 --> 00:01:09.543
There it binds a receptor called RAR.

15
00:01:10.443 --> 00:01:15.363
The receptor pairs with another one, RXR, on a short stretch of DNA.

16
00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:19.823
Hoxa1 and Hoxb1 carry such stretches.

17
00:01:20.683 --> 00:01:23.243
When the pair sits there, the gene comes on.

18
00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:28.673
Hox genes sit in a row on a chromosome, and they obey a rule.

19
00:01:29.273 --> 00:01:33.893
Their order along the chromosome matches the order of their front edges along the

20
00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:37.993
body. Genes at the 3′ end reach farthest forward.

21
00:01:38.673 --> 00:01:41.493
Genes toward the 5′ end stop farther back.

22
00:01:42.413 --> 00:01:47.853
In cells in a dish, 3′ genes respond to lower doses of retinoic acid.

23
00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:53.233
So where the signal is lower, fewer genes come on, and they are the 3′ ones.

24
00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:58.507
Each rhombomere ends up with its own mix of Hox proteins.

25
00:01:59.287 --> 00:02:01.067
That mix is its address.

26
00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:04.347
It decides which nerve the segment builds.

27
00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:10.567
In the chick, r2 and r3 make the trigeminal nerve, for chewing.

28
00:02:11.607 --> 00:02:15.627
R4 and r5 make the facial nerve, for facial expression.

29
00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.520
Now change the signal.

30
00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:25.320
In mouse embryos given extra retinoic acid early, the Hox domains changed.

31
00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:31.540
Rhombomeres 2 and 3 were transformed toward the identity of 4 and 5.

32
00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:34.640
The address follows the signal.

33
00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:40.920
In early pregnancy, extra retinoic acid shifts the Hox code of the hindbrain.

34
00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:45.140
That fits how a pill for the skin can disturb the face.

35
00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:49.200
Too little vitamin A harms the embryo as well.

36
00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:52.560
The dose has to be right in both directions.
